 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Luigi Mangione appears at a pretrial hearing in Manhattan Criminal Court on Tuesday. Photo: David Dee Delgado/Pool via Getty Images ⚖️ Luigi Mangione is expected to plead guilty tomorrow to federal stalking charges tied to the killing of UnitedHealthcare CEO Brian Thompson, The New York Times reports. Mangione is also facing trial on a murder charge in New York State. If he pleads guilty in federal court, his lawyers may argue that New York's double jeopardy laws prevent a murder trial tied to the same event. Gift link . ⚓️ The Pentagon is sending the aircraft carrier USS George Washington to the Middle East to replace the USS Abraham Lincoln, The Wall Street Journal reports. The Abraham Lincoln has been at sea for a record 200 days, and lawmakers and others have raised concerns about conditions aboard the ship. Gift link . 📺 American Action Network, a top outside group aligned with House GOP leaders, is launching a $22 million ad campaign across 41 congressional districts. Scoop from Stef W. Kight . 💰 A Powerball ticket sold at a western Illinois gas station was the sole winner of last night's $1 billion jackpot. Go deeper . 
 
